d's hair and make some  tears in his clothes some might have  been shocked by the fact that Sirius  Black was a member of the Gryffindor  House back in the day Sirius is  reputation as a prisoner of azkaban  definitely preceded him his appearance  got the better of him too as he was  described in the books as being bony  skeleton like and crazed looking due to  his hard life he also had dirty long  hair that fell to his elbows sunken eyes  oily skin and yellow teeth in the books  Sirius is definitely one scary-looking  guy but he had good intentions to help  Harry as he was an old friend of Harry's  father James Gary Oldman captured the  appearance quite well but was lacking  other aspects of Sirius as sickly  appearance he also lacked of the long  hair and skeletal look before Minerva  McGonagall was a professor at Hogwarts  she attended the school and was sorted  into the Gryffindor House Minerva is  described as having black hair that she  rarely let down and was intense looking  she often looked prim and pursed her  lips occasionally she would let loose  whereby she appeared to be an entirely  different person Maggie Smith did an  amazing job of capturing Minerva's  appearance and personality although she  was described as younger looking in the  books compared to the movies one detail  they forgot to include was Minerva  square spectacles Minerva often wore  these glasses to match the markings of  her animagus and Patronus which was a  silver tabby cat this is a minor detail  otherwise the cast and crew did an  excellent job Seamus Finnigan is one of  Harry Potter's quirkier characters and a  member of the Gryffindor House  in the books Seamus is described as  having an Irish accent sandy colored  hair and a sloppy appearance he also has  an impeccable knack for making things  explode by a mistake  Devin Murray did a good job with the  Irish accent and sloppy clothes in the  movie he's often blowing things up by  mistake in the movies leaving his face  covered 